# Copy to .env and uncomment what you need. With everything left commented
# out, `npm run dev` runs on the local stand-in (any login works, no data).

# Which data backend to use (sign-in and data). The app is not tied to any
# backend:
#   custom   = your own backend, through the adapter you write in
#              src/integrations/data/customClient.ts
#   supabase = (default) a Supabase project, set with the two lines below
# VITE_BACKEND_PROVIDER=custom

# Only when using Supabase.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://<your-project-ref>.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<your-supabase-anon-key>

# Trading, wallet/payments and audit events. Setting these makes the app
# send real requests.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_MIDDLEWARE_WS_URL=wss://api.example.com/ws
